#: dist/events-made-easy/includes/eme-actions.php:591
#: includes/eme-actions.php:591
msgid "<p>Hey, <strong>%1$s</strong>, welcome to <strong>Events Made Easy</strong>! We hope you like it around here.</p><p>Now it's time to insert events lists through <a href='%2$s' title='%3$s'>widgets</a>, <a href='%4$s' title='%5$s'>template tags</a> or <a href='%6$s' title='%7$s'>shortcodes</a>.</p><p>By the way, have you taken a look at the <a href='%8$s' title='%9$s'>Settings page</a>? That's where you customize the way events and locations are displayed.</p><p>What? Tired of seeing this advice? I hear you, <a href='#' class='eme-dismiss-notice' data-notice='hello' title='%10$s'>click here</a> and you won't see this again!</p>"
msgstr "<p>Hi, <strong>%1$s</strong>, welkom bij <strong>Evenents Made Easy</strong>! We hopen dat je het hier naar je zin hebt.</p><p>Nu is het tijd om evenementenlijsten in te voegen via <a href='%2$s' title='%3$s'>widgets</a>, <a href='%4$s' title='%5$s'>sjabloontags</a> of <a href='%6$s' title='%7$s'>shortcodes</a>.</p><p>Trouwens, heb je al eens gekeken naar de <a href='%8$s' title='%9$s'>Instellingenpagina</a>? Daar kun je aanpassen hoe evenementen en locaties worden weergegeven.</p><p>Wat? Moe van dit advies? Ik snap het, <a href='#' class='eme-dismiss-notice' data-notice='hello' title='%10$s'>klik hier</a> en je ziet dit niet meer!</p>"

